{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","index":0,"message":{"content":"I have a strong lead. Let me verify the key facts:\n\n1. Chigozie Obioma was born in Akure, Nigeria (confirmed in e1)\n2. His novels \"The Fishermen\" (2015) and \"An Orchestra of Minorities\" (2019) were shortlisted for the Booker Prize and translated into 30 languages (confirmed in e1)\n3. The International Booker Prize was established in 2005 (the 2000s) - confirmed in e2 and search results\n\nNow I need to verify the connection. The question says: \"In the 2010s, the year in which this book was published, another book, which had been released the preceding year, won the very award above for which the first book was later in contention.\"\n\n\"An Orchestra of Minorities\" was published in 2019 and shortlisted for the 2019 Booker Prize. The 2019 Booker Prize was won jointly by Margaret Atwood (\"The Testaments\") and Bernardine Evaristo (\"Girl, Woman, Other\"). \"Girl, Woman, Other\" was published in May 2019, and \"The Testaments\" was published in September 2019.\n\nWait - the question says the award was \"originally created in the 2000s.\" The Booker Prize was created in 1969, but the International Booker Prize was created in 2005. Let me reconsider whether the award in question is the International Booker Prize or the regular Booker Prize.\n\nLet me check the Man Asian Literary Prize angle too, and verify Bernardine Evaristo's birthplace.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"ref\": \"d75\"}","name":"read"},"id":"call_f5cf44fd66934d49ba5b6675","index":0,"type":"function"},{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Bernardine Evaristo born London Eltham birthplace\", \"Chigozie Obioma grew up Akure childhood biography\", \"An Orchestra of Minorities published 2019 Booker Prize shortlisted\"], \"top_k\": 10}","name":"search"},"id":"call_5977c4a35b024700b28bbad5","index":1,"type":"function"}]}}],"created":1789476855,"id":"chatcmpl-dfea1175-6cf8-9303-ac2a-fd71669058